 "lines": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "text": "What if the United States got mad and wanted to take the entire world?",
   "s": 0.0,
   "e": 3.84
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "text": "It starts with Canada. And Israel signs up for the mission.",
   "s": 4.5,
   "e": 8.1
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "text": "Canada has about 65,000 active troops guarding the second-largest country on Earth. It falls in a week.",
   "s": 9.16,
   "e": 15.62
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "text": "But the UN gets mad. Emergency session. Sanctions. The whole world turns on America.",
   "s": 16.08,
   "e": 22.0
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "text": "The US doesn't care. It rolls straight through Canada, all the way north to Greenland.",
   "s": 22.56,
   "e": 27.4
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "text": "Denmark tries to stop them, with the UN right behind it.",
   "s": 28.2,
   "e": 31.58
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "text": "The US plows straight through.",
   "s": 31.82,
   "e": 33.48
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "text": "Then Mexico and Central America fall in days, and American carriers start crossing the Atlantic.",
   "s": 34.12,
   "e": 39.56
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "text": "That's when Russia and China team up. Now it's two thirds of the planet against one superpower.",
   "s": 40.24,
   "e": 45.8
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "text": "America has 11 supercarriers. No other country has more than 3. It could win almost every battle.",
   "s": 46.62,
   "e": 53.0
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "text": "But no army in history has ever held 8 billion people. Should I make part 2?",
   "s": 53.0,
   "e": 58.68
  }
 ],
 "heard": "What if the United States got mad and wanted to take the entire world? It starts with Canada. And Israel signs up for the mission. Canada has about 65 ,000 active troops guarding the second -largest country on Earth. It falls in a week. But the UN gets mad. Emergency session. Sanctions. The whole world turns on America. The US doesn't care. It rolls straight through Canada, all the way north to Greenland. Denmark tries to stop them, with the UN right behind it. The US plows straight through. Then Mexico and Central America fall in days, and American carriers start crossing the Atlantic. That's when Russia and China team up. Now it's two thirds of the planet against one superpower. America has 11 supercarriers. No other country has more than 3. It could win almost every battle. But no army in history has ever held 8 billion people. Should I make part two?"
}